+    num_decodes * decode.max_query_len`` -> ``q.view(num_decodes, -1, H, D)``), so
+    every batch this accepts is one the stock path runs as a uniform block, with
+    the same per-token causal bound inside the kernel. A ragged block (adaptive
+    drafting) returns 0: the stock path flattens it per token and does not return
+    an LSE row per request there, so it keeps the stock collectives."""
